r"],"finding":"The new endpoint/provider scoped fuse is a circuit-breaker variant, but the plan neither names the standard circuit-breaker pattern nor justifies why its bespoke multi-dimensional scoping (per-(provider,endpoint) identity, 3-consecutive-across-≥2-tickets threshold, provider-requires-≥2-endpoints, per-pass in-memory counters) is needed over an established per-endpoint breaker or an existing resilience library.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f113211d9ba0c95ce","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan step 3 and 'Fuse scope, eligibility & counter semantics (resolves E2/G6)' section","norm_id":"ne9080d696028316a","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Reviewer/maintainer cannot tell whether the bespoke threshold shape (2-ticket + 2-endpoint gates) is a considered refinement over a standard breaker or an under-analyzed invention","A future contributor reaches for pybreaker/tenacity and duplicates state the fuse already tracks"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"In step 3 or the fuse-semantics section, state explicitly that the fuse is a circuit-breaker specialization, cite the established pattern and one representative library, and explain the delta: outcome-typed eligibility (only exhausted_transient / terminal retryable_deferred), authoritative-scope short-circuit independent of counters, and the 2-ticket/2-endpoint gates that a stock breaker lacks — mirroring how ADR 0103 and check_blast_radius already document their prior-art deltas.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2857,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_att